---
/**
 * Landing page (marketing-site story 2, CAP-1). Copy is drawn from CONTEXT
 * §1–§3 and describes what the product is designed to do. Every guarded
 * phrase sits inside its `<Capability>`, so it carries a visible status badge
 * and the build-time site check passes. The title, description and OG text
 * carry no guarded phrase, because metadata cannot carry a badge.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Capability from "../components/Capability.astro";

const grid = "mt-4 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3";
const item = "rounded border border-slate-200 p-3";
const h3 = "inline font-semibold";
const body = "mt-1 text-sm text-slate-700";
const secondaryLink = "font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-slate-700";
---

<Base
  title="Sanitization proof you can check yourself (pre-launch)"
  description="Wipestation is a pre-launch data sanitization product, designed around certificates that carry their own evidence and that anyone with the public key can check."
>
  <section aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <p class="inline-block rounded bg-amber-100 px-2 py-1 text-sm font-semibold text-amber-950">
      Pre-launch: Wipestation is not on sale yet, and every pre-release build runs against
      simulated drives.
    </p>
    <h1 id="hero-title" class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
      The proof is in the certificate.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-lg text-slate-700">
      Wipestation is data sanitization software for ITAD benches and enterprise IT, designed to
      <Capability id="drive-sanitization">sanitize SSDs and HDDs to NIST Clear or Purge</Capability>
      and to hand you
      <Capability id="offline-verification"
        >a certificate that carries its own evidence, which anyone with the public key can
        check</Capability
      >.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
      <a
        href="/early-access/"
        data-cta="primary"
        class="inline-block rounded bg-slate-900 px-5 py-2.5 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-slate-700"
        >Join early access</a
      >
      <a href="/capabilities/" class={secondaryLink}>See the status of every capability</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="problem">
    <h2 id="problem" class="text-xl font-semibold">The problem: proof that is hard to defend</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 max-w-prose list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-slate-700">
      <li>
        Most certificates are prose attached to a serial number, not the commands issued and the
        status they returned.
      </li>
      <li>
        Authenticity is usually checked against the vendor's database. If that service is gone, so
        is the proof.
      </li>
      <li>
        Some tools bill when a job starts, whatever the outcome; some shops budget 10–15% extra
        licence headroom for jobs that fail.
      </li>
      <li>Many tools advertise NVMe support but quietly fall back to a plain overwrite.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="certificate">
    <h2 id="certificate" class="text-xl font-semibold">A certificate anyone can check</h2>
    <ul class={grid}>
      <Capability id="offline-verification" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Offline-verifiable</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed so anyone with the public key can verify a certificate without contacting the
          vendor, via an Ed25519 signature.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="command-level-evidence" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Command-level evidence</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed to record each issued opcode, its status and the log pages read. Proof, not
          prose.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="open-cert-format" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Open certificate format</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          The JSON-LD certificate schema is to be published, so anyone can build a verifier.
        </p>
      </Capability>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="different">
    <h2 id="different" class="text-xl font-semibold">Why it is different</h2>
    <ul class={grid}>
      <Capability id="outcome-bearing-job" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>One certificate per asset</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed to compose every attempt on an asset, retries included, into one signed
          certificate.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="per-success-licensing" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Per-success licensing</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Built to spend a licence credit only on a verified success; failures and re-runs are
          free.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="nvme-sanitize" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>Honest NVMe Sanitize</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed to issue NVMe Sanitize first, with an explicit fallback order and no quiet
          overwrite.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="hpa-dco-clear" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>HPA/DCO cleared before Purge</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed to clear HPA and DCO hidden regions first, and refuse to report Purge otherwise.
        </p>
      </Capability>
      <Capability id="erp-integration" as="li" badge="start" class={item}>
        <h3 class={h3}>ERP integration first</h3>
        <p class={body}>
          Designed for REST in and out and webhooks on job changes, so your ERP stays the system of
          record.
        </p>
      </Capability>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="not">
    <h2 id="not" class="text-xl font-semibold">What we are not</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 max-w-prose list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-slate-700">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">Not per-event billing with a new logo.</strong> It is
        designed to replace
        <Capability id="per-success-licensing">per-event billing with per-success licensing</Capability>
        and to add
        <Capability id="offline-verification">offline-verifiable certificates</Capability>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">Not a hobbyist tool.</strong> We target compliance
        procurement, with
        <Capability id="adisa-al5">ADISA AL5</Capability> and
        <Capability id="common-criteria-eal2">Common Criteria EAL 2</Capability> as the
        <Capability id="independent-certification">target certification floor</Capability>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-slate-900">Not a destruction-only product.</strong> We model the
        destroy path, with
        <Capability id="destruction-attestation"
          >operator attestation and a chain of custody</Capability
        >, but the primary value is in Clear and Purge.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8 rounded border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4" aria-labelledby="join">
    <h2 id="join" class="text-xl font-semibold">Early access</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-slate-700">
      For ITAD operators and enterprise IT teams who want to try pre-release builds against
      simulated drives and shape what ships first.
      <a href="/early-access/" class={secondaryLink}>How early access works</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
